@model WorkshopModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Storage & migration"; }
<h1>The dashboard ships with the app.</h1><p class="lead">Precompiled Razor pages, local assets, the existing .NET evaluator and your selected storage provider.</p>
<section class="card"><h2>Observe the full lifecycle</h2><ol><li>Change a rule in <a href="/internal/features">the dashboard</a>. A successful write creates a revision and updates this writer's runtime.</li><li>Refresh a workshop page to evaluate again. Other hosts sharing storage poll every five seconds by default.</li><li>Stop and restart the app from the same directory with the same SQLite file. Your catalog remains.</li><li>Disable a targeted feature, <a href="/internal/features/export">export it</a>, and enable it again. Its stored rules are retained.</li></ol><p>Active revision: <code>@(Model.Revision ?? "none")</code>. The <a href="/internal/features/storage">storage page</a> reports current state. After schema setup succeeds, an initial runtime catalog-read failure leaves flags off. Later refresh failures retain the last valid snapshot; the runtime does not reset a missing or invalid catalog.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Deployment boundary</h2><p>This sample defaults to direct loopback dashboard access. Remote requests, including requests with forwarding headers, require an explicit host authorization policy. Add your real authentication middleware and <code>.RequireAuthorization("FeatureAdmins")</code>; demo identity controls are not a login system.</p><p>Use persistent storage, host Data Protection settings and the catalog-only schema scripts for existing databases. The sample's explicit <code>EnsureCreatedAsync()</code> creates a missing dedicated SQLite database and schema; a schema setup failure aborts startup. If the database file is lost, restore its backup before restarting, or this sample will create an empty database.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Move to Toggly Cloud when you need it</h2><p><a href="/internal/features/cloud">Open the packaged migration instructions</a>. Export, import into an existing SaaS application/environment, resolve conflicts and approvals, and verify publication. Configure a backend SDK key, replace the embedded registration with <code>AddTogglyWeb()</code>, preserve identity/context registration, and remove the dashboard mapping.</p><p>Keep the local catalog backup for rollback. Never register local and cloud definition providers together. No network connection is initiated by viewing these instructions.</p></section>
